(A) Remark 3.2': the three-point example (0,10), (1,5), (2,0)
  zero-window left kink of steepness 5 at (1,5): True; steepness 5+1/1000: False
  zero-window right kink of flatness 5 at (1,5): True; flatness 5-1/1000: False
  (1,5) extreme point of conv + R^2_+ (i.e. a hull vertex): False; (0,10): True; (2,0): True
  lambda =    4: MAP points [(2, Fraction(0, 1))]
  lambda =  9/2: MAP points [(2, Fraction(0, 1))]
  lambda =    5: MAP points [(0, Fraction(10, 1)), (1, Fraction(5, 1)), (2, Fraction(0, 1))]
  lambda = 11/2: MAP points [(0, Fraction(10, 1))]
  lambda =    6: MAP points [(0, Fraction(10, 1))]
  strictness, explicit: left kink (5, w=0) at (2,0) of {(0,10),(2,0)}: MAP set at lambda = 5 is [(0, Fraction(10, 1)), (2, Fraction(0, 1))] (a MAP of length 0 < 2)
  strictness, explicit: right kink (5, w=0) at (0,10) of the same set: MAP set at lambda = 5 contains (2,0), length 2 > 0
