(B) Thm 3.2(a)-(d) on random classes, windows included (exact); the counts behind Remark 3.2'
  left kinks tested: 2632 (two-part bound checked 9040 times); right kinks: 5879; no violation of (a), (b) (asserted)
  zero-window kinks with tau < sigma: 926, all vertices with the MAP set as stated (asserted)
  zero-window kinks at (alpha, rho(alpha)) with tau = sigma (best constants): 13, of which vertices: 0
  at lambda = sigma a MAP lies left of alpha - w in 563 cases; at lambda = tau a MAP lies right of alpha + w in 556 cases
  vertices: 3228; zero-window kinks with tau < sigma there: 3228 (converse of (d))
====================================================================================================
(C) Prop 3.5(ii): a universal member U (F_U <= F + l + kappa0 for every program) caps every lambda-MAP
  28000 (class, lambda) cases: violations of l(MAP) <= (lambda l_U + kappa0)/(lambda - 1): 0 (0 required); bound attained with equality in 493 cases
  'at most l_U + (l_U+kappa0)/eps exactly when lambda >= 1 + eps': checked in 82740 cases with l_U + kappa0 > 0
  degenerate case l_U = kappa0 = 0: the bound is 0 for every lambda > 1, so 'at most l_U + 0/eps' holds also for lambda < 1 + eps; the 'exactly when' clause needs l_U + kappa0 > 0
  sharpness: l_U=3, kappa0=1, lambda=2: bound 7; class {(3,100), (7,92)} satisfies (Dom); MAP points [(3, Fraction(100, 1)), (7, Fraction(92, 1))]
====================================================================================================
(D) Cor 5.7(d), deterministic step: if the lambda-MAPs occupy a single point, it is a vertex v_i with
    sigma_{i+1} < lambda < sigma_i; its largest right secant (floored at 0) equals the next edge slope
  15979 (class, lambda) cases with a single MAP point (3999 at lambda = 1): all vertices with s_+ = sigma_(i+1) < lambda < sigma_i <= s_- (asserted): 15979
